SIMPLE  =                    T / Fits standard                                  
BITPIX  =                  -32 / Bits per pixel                                 
NAXIS   =                    1 / Number of dimensions                           
NAXIS1  =                 2048 / Length of axis                                 
COMMENT Vacuum wavelength axis for a grism operated in air.  Grism parameters   
COMMENT are those of the KPNO MARS grism in FITS-WCS Paper III Fig. 5, with     
COMMENT the non-zero epsilon and theta that WCSLIB's tspc.c adds to them.       
CTYPE1  = 'WAVE-GRA'           / Vacuum wavelength, grism in air                
CUNIT1  = 'm       '           / Axis units                                     
CRPIX1  =                719.8 / [pixel] Reference pixel                        
CRVAL1  =            7.2472E-7 / [m] Reference vacuum wavelength                
CDELT1  =            2.956E-10 / [m/pixel] Dispersion                           
PV1_0   =             450000.0 / [m^(-1)] G: grating ruling density             
PV1_1   =                  1.0 / m: diffraction order                           
PV1_2   =                 27.0 / [deg] alpha: angle of incidence                
PV1_3   =                1.765 / n_r: refractive index at reference             
PV1_4   =           -1077000.0 / [m^(-1)] n'_r: dn/dlambda at reference         
PV1_5   =                  3.0 / [deg] epsilon: grating tilt                    
PV1_6   =                  5.0 / [deg] theta: detector tilt                     
SPECSYS = 'HELIOCEN'           / Standard of rest for spectral axis             
VELOSYS =            29336.889 / [m/s] Topo. apparent velocity of rest frame    
END                                                                             
